    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `timezone` field to the owner response, derived from the locality/region via the fixed table (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane).\n\nThree small, cohesive changes:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `timezone` string field to the owner schema (this generates `OwnerDto`).\n2. **`Locality.java`** (small, low-context class) \u2014 added a `REGION_TIMEZONE` table and a one-line `timezone(String region)` lookup returning the IANA name, or `null` for unlisted regions.\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a single `@Mapping` line for `timezone` that reuses the exact same region resolution as the existing `locality` mapping (customer-code prefix, else `Locality.of(city, postcode)`), so the two fields always agree.\n\nI kept structural impact low by putting the new logic in the tiny `Locality` class rather than growing the many-method `OwnerMapper`, and by touching each changed function with a single line. The new `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` and the full suite are green.",
